== Correction before commit: the log test did not yet cover what the plan says ==
Checking the verdicts against B8_PLAN.md before committing: design section 6 says the log test covers a successful
analysis and each failure path of section 5. test_no_log_line_carries_a_genotype_or_an_identifier covered the success
path and three failures (non-zero exit with a report, no output, unreadable report). A verdict drafted on that test was
withdrawn before commit. The test now covers, with the uploaded filename and a planted sample ID in play:
  through /analyze: success (real PharmCAT, 200); a failure while building the response (real PharmCAT, 500); no engine,
  i.e. before PharmCAT starts; a non-zero exit with a report; an unreadable report; no output; a timeout (all 503);
  through the runner: a cancellation, with the sample hint /analyze passes (TestClient cannot cancel a request).
It asserts each of those statuses, so a path that silently did not run fails the test. It checks each record as an
operator log shows it (message and any traceback), and everything written to stdout/stderr during the run (capfd). The
positive control now plants a leak in a message (5 found), in a traceback only (1) and in raw output only (1).
Sabotage re-run on the extended test (partb/B8.sabotage.stdout, replacing the earlier run): SB8-a..f all caught, every
file restored identical; SB8-d now turns 3 tests red (the log test's status check is the third). SB8-g, added beyond the
plan, has main.py print the uploaded filename: caught by the log test (1 red), restored identical.
The application code is unchanged by this; the zero-regression and container runs above stand.
