Stage 2, environment (owner-approved Render API write):
E1  Before the write: the values of CLIENT_IP_HEADER, MAX_WAITING_UPLOADS and TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS (none is a secret),
    and one sha256 over every other key and value (no other value printed).
E2  Written in this order: CLIENT_IP_HEADER=cf-connecting-ip, MAX_WAITING_UPLOADS=2, then TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=
    10.0.0.0/8 last, because with the CIDR set and no header the code keys on the first X-Forwarded-For entry, which
    a client can forge. Read back: the three values exactly; the digest over every other key and value unchanged.
E3  Render's deploy list read before and after the write: whether the write itself started a deploy is recorded,
    not assumed.
E4  The Deploy workflow re-run (workflow_dispatch on main, 6d0e964): gate, Render and Cloudflare succeed; /ready
    reports 6d0e964f28463271485c29f10c128af784c02123.
Then, with no upload from this machine since that deploy went live (the limiter lives in the process, so a new
deploy starts it empty):
L4-i   Eleven /coverage uploads from this machine, one after another, within 300 s: the eleventh gets 429. Every
       status is recorded; the first ten are expected to answer 200.
L4-ii  Then one more with a forged CF-Connecting-IP: 192.0.2.77 (TEST-NET-1): still 429.
L4-iii The same with a forged X-Forwarded-For: 192.0.2.78: still 429.
L4-iv  If L4-i fails, the header is absent; if L4-ii fails, it is forgeable. Either way the environment change is
       rolled back (TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS removed first, which alone restores today's keys, then the other two to their
       E1 values), the Deploy workflow re-run, and it is reported; never left half-working.
L5 (beyond the plan) L4-i to iii would also pass if the key were one Render hop that every request happened to
       share. So, positively: after at least 300 s with no upload from this machine, while one /analyze of S1 runs,
       a /coverage from this machine gets 429 ONE_AT_A_TIME with Retry-After. The server answers that only when the
       peer is a trusted proxy and CF-Connecting-IP holds exactly one valid address. If it does not, L4-iv applies.
No address is logged or recorded: only statuses, error codes and Retry-After.
